  "note": "Regenerated 2026-10-16 after verilator-harness-absolute fix (commit 37ab63f): perf_main.cpp harness path now uses absolute CPPHDL_PERF_HARNESS_DIR injected by CMake, cache_root/workdir absolute-ized at main() start, and the missing-file branch was split into two else-if with distinct reasons. Net effect: TC-07/08 verilator rows are PASS for the first time since baseline was introduced; previously they were SKIPPED \"verilog or harness file missing\" because subprocess_runner.h chdir'd the child to a per-TC temp dir and the relative \"build/tests/...\" harness paths resolved against the wrong cwd. TC-09/11 verilator rows remain SKIPPED with reason \"verilator harness not implemented\" (no harness file exists; TC-11 is also blocked by the 64-bit port cap per AGENTS.md VERILATOR BACKEND RULES). F2 isolated baseline, regenerated 2026-06-23 after F2 subprocess dispatch landed. TC-07/08/09 run in fresh child processes via subprocess_runner.h; TC-10/11 run in-process in the parent (no other TCs have polluted the ORC JIT state). Per-backend thresholds: interpreter 2.5x, jit 1.6x, verilator 1.3x. TC-09 rows are SKIPPED because subprocess_runner.h 180s timeout is insufficient for ch_uint<32> arith chain depth=1000 (~30M us jit exceeds budget). See openspec/changes/archive/2026-06-19-fix-perf-subprocess-isolation/ and docs/developer_guide/tech-reports/perf-report-todo.md W12 for context. Predecessor: 92e7fe6 (polluted state, pre-F2 dispatch) \u2014 replaced because current code (c1e08e4 + 2f0ce28) measures TC-11 in clean ORC state, which is ~2-3x slower than the polluted predecessor baseline."
